From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <darknagel@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:35:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] temp/modemmanager: do not abort when the modem is recreated

ModemManager 0007: the data port reset during initialization also took
the ignored mhi_swip0 port of the SDX55, and the qcom-soc plugin
asserts that a data port is in the net subsystem. Without a SIM,
ModemManager recreates the modem after every resume and aborted each
time.
---
 ...-modem-qmi-reset-only-real-net-ports.patch | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
 temp/modemmanager/APKBUILD                    |  4 ++-
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 temp/modemmanager/0007-broadband-modem-qmi-reset-only-real-net-ports.patch

diff --git a/temp/modemmanager/0007-broadband-modem-qmi-reset-only-real-net-ports.patch b/temp/modemmanager/0007-broadband-modem-qmi-reset-only-real-net-ports.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..e917d38a06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/temp/modemmanager/0007-broadband-modem-qmi-reset-only-real-net-ports.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:21:45 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] broadband-modem-qmi: reset only real net ports
+
+An explicitly ignored port is grabbed as a plain MMPort with its port
+type but without a subsystem. The data port reset during
+initialization looked for net ports of any subsystem and so also got
+the ignored mhi_swip0 of the SDX55, and the qcom-soc plugin asserts
+that a data port is in the net subsystem: ModemManager aborted each
+time it recreated the modem, for example after every resume without a
+SIM ("new SIM detected, handle as SIM hot-swap").
+
+Look only for net ports in the net subsystem.
+---
+ src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c | 4 +++-
+ 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+index 9620504..7d8d0da 100644
+--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
++++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+@@ -14572,8 +14572,10 @@ reset_ports (MMBroadbandModemQmi *self,
+     ctx = g_slice_new0 (ResetPortsContext);
+     g_task_set_task_data (task, ctx, (GDestroyNotify)reset_ports_context_free);
+ 
++    /* Only real net ports: an explicitly ignored port is grabbed with its
++     * type but without a subsystem, and asking for its QMI port asserts. */
+     ctx->ports = mm_base_modem_find_ports (MM_BASE_MODEM (self),
+-                                           MM_PORT_SUBSYS_UNKNOWN,
++                                           MM_PORT_SUBSYS_NET,
+                                            MM_PORT_TYPE_NET);
+ 
+     reset_next_port (task);
diff --git a/temp/modemmanager/APKBUILD b/temp/modemmanager/APKBUILD
index 5265b351a5..0ee7dcbfb7 100644
--- a/temp/modemmanager/APKBUILD
+++ b/temp/modemmanager/APKBUILD
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
